\uc0\u55357 \u56538  Review \'97 Light\'92s Out by Richard DeVeau\
\
Light\'92s Out is a razor-sharp, adrenaline-fueled thriller that grabs you from its chilling opening scene and refuses to let go. Richard DeVeau delivers a gripping fusion of domestic terrorism, political corruption, and psychological intrigue\'97crafted with a pace and precision that fans of high-stakes thrillers will devour.\
\
The novel opens with two seemingly unrelated catastrophes: a Wisconsin couple murdered in their home and an oil tanker exploding on Lake Michigan. Enter Eve Tuant\'97special forces veteran, CIA operative, and the formidable leader of Boston\'92s Homeland Security team. Brilliant, relentless, and deeply human, Eve becomes the anchor of this electrifying story as she pieces together a pattern most would overlook.\
\
Her target? A terrifying antagonist: an M.I.T.-trained missile expert with military polish and the cold, calculated cruelty of a serial killer. But the conspiracy runs deeper than one man. Eve soon uncovers a cabal of influential leaders, including a sitting U.S. senator, orchestrating a series of escalating attacks capable of devastating the nation.\
\
Fast-paced, tightly plotted, and disturbingly plausible, Light\'92s Out is a must-read for fans of political thrillers, military suspense, and heroes who fight in the shadows to protect a nation on the brink.\
